error[E1010]: this closure captured `ch`, which reaches a channel that carries bytes, and it is returned here: whoever calls it next may hand it bytes that are freed before a receiver could ever use them
 --> mem:///main.lu:3:5
  |
3 |     f
  |     ^ a closure that may send on `ch` leaves its frame
  |
  = note: a closure that captured a channel sends what it is called with, and a fn value's type
    does not say what it captured — once it leaves the frame that made it, no call of it can
    be checked [conc.chan.payload] [mem.region.escape]. Call the closure where it was made,
    or hand over the channel itself and let the other side send: a channel argument is
    checked at every call that passes it.
